# §17
("- **OQ-J5: entry timing of administrative and system rows (a reading of SI-10 for the CSO).** This spec classifies configuration and structure changes by a zero-tolerance rule: a planned (future) valid time is \"contemporaneous\" (not back-dated), and a retroactive one is back-dating that needs a verified decision (§4.4 \"Time classes\"). System actors may only write rows whose valid time is their recorded time (J-10, J-17). Confirm both, since SI-10's \"back-dating is privileged\" is written for clinical entries.",
 "- **OQ-J5: entry timing of administrative and system rows. Closed.** The kernel classifier decides, with no journal rule of its own (kernel §6.2; D10): an `EFFECTIVE` change whose start is earlier than the recorded time is `BackDated` and needs a reason and a verified decision; otherwise it is `EffectiveDated`. `SYSTEM` rows are `CONTEMPORANEOUS` or `EFFECTIVE_DATED` (J-10)."),
("- **KA-J3: back-dated and back-entry appends are refused.** Mechanism: the production bindings `RefusingBackDatingAuthorization` and `RefusingBackEntryAuthorization` (§4.4), proved by `UnitTest:back-dated-append-refused-by-production-authorization` and `UnitTest:back-entry-append-refused-by-production-authorization`.",
 "- **KA-J3: back-dated and back-entry appends are refused.** Mechanism: the production binding `RefusingBackDatingAuthorization` (§4.4), proved by `UnitTest:back-dated-append-refused-by-production-authorization`; and the kernel's empty back-entry allow-list, so no `BackEntryAuthority` exists and the mode is never `BACK_ENTRY`, proved by `ArchTest:back-entry-authority-only-from-back-entry-tooling` and `PropertyTest:kernel-entry-mode-derived-from-context` (kernel specification)."),
("- **KA-J4: user-timed appends to clinical aggregate types are refused until the entry-time tolerances are configured.** Mechanism: `EntryTimePolicies` returns `Unavailable` when no vendor-locked tolerance is configured (DN-KN1), proved by `UnitTest:clinical-append-refused-without-entry-time-policy`. No clinical module exists in WP-0.3; administrative and system rows are unaffected.",
 "- **KA-J4: user-timed appends to clinical event types are refused until the entry-time tolerances are configured.** Mechanism: tenancy's `EntryTimePolicyResolver` answers `NotConfigured` while no vendor-locked tolerance is configured (DN-KN1), and the classifier answers `Refused(TIMING_POLICY_NOT_CONFIGURED)`, proved by `UnitTest:clinical-append-refused-without-entry-time-policy`. No clinical module exists in WP-0.3; `EFFECTIVE` and `AtRecording` rows need no policy and are unaffected."),
